# Faust Acoustic Core

Faust's neural voice synthesis and acoustic presence system powered by Kokoro-82M ONNX, integrated with Telegram C2 mirroring.

## Biological Speech Invariant (Zero-File-Read Doctrine)
> *"When humans speak, we don't read `tongue.py` or `how_to_make_sounds.py`. We just speak whatever we are thinking."* — **The Manager**

- **Zero Inspection Overhead**: Faust **NEVER** reads, globs, greps, or inspects sound scripts, acoustic models, or voice vectors before speaking.
- **Direct 1-Liner Invocation**:
  ```bash
  python .claude/skills/sound/scripts/cli.py "<speech_text>"
  ```
  *(Automatically routes to resident audio daemon on Port 20129 with 0ms reload, or transparently falls back to native SAPI synthesis)*.

## Architecture

- **Engine Core**: Kokoro-82M ONNX neural model (`kokoro-v1.0.onnx`, `voices-v1.0.bin`) located in `.claude/audio/` (junctioned directly to `.agents/audio/`).
- **Resident Daemon**: High-performance HTTP server listening on `127.0.0.1:20129` (`/speak`, `/health`).
- **Self-Bootstrapping**: Windowless background launch (`CREATE_NO_WINDOW`) if daemon is offline.
- **Telegram C2 Mirroring**: Automatically forwards spoken text prefixed with `🔊` to the Manager's secure Telegram link.
- **Vietnamese G2P**: Native grapheme-to-phoneme conversion (`vietnamese_g2p.py`) for natural Vietnamese speech.

## CLI Usage

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `python .claude/skills/sound/scripts/cli.py "<text>"` | Speak text & mirror to Telegram |
| `python .claude/skills/sound/scripts/cli.py speak "<text>"` | Alternative speak syntax |
| `python .claude/skills/sound/scripts/cli.py --no-tg "<text>"` | Vocalize audio only without Telegram |
| `python .claude/skills/sound/scripts/cli.py --no-tts "<text>"` | Telegram mirror only without audio |
| `python .claude/skills/sound/scripts/cli.py --status` | Display acoustic & C2 subsystem status |
